# Swan Compiler 2 — IR Generation
#
# Lower verified SIL into the lower-level, target-independent SVM input IR.
# This stage is analogous to Swift IRGen's lowering boundary, but emits Swan's
# own IR rather than LLVM IR.
#
# Responsibilities:
# - Lower SIL control flow, calls, values, and memory operations.
# - Erase high-level abstractions only after their semantics are represented.
# - Make data layout and ABI-dependent choices explicit inputs, not globals.
# - Preserve debug locations and source-level symbol identity.
# - Reject SIL operations with no defined SVM lowering.
#
# Output: typed SVM IR with explicit control flow and SSA definitions.
# Output must pass IR verification before SVM generation.
#
# Implementation status: contract; the current swanc/ir/IR.swan is only an
# early linear IR format and is not yet a complete SIL lowering target.
